WEBVTT

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:02.980
Sohoku.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.900
You made it. I'm impressed.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.730
No wonder you two brought so much 
excitement to last year's Inter-High.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:09.890
No way.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:13.110
I caused way more excitement 
than him, honestly.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:13.110
I caused way more excitement 
than him, definitely.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.370
Could you not group us together?

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.870
Don't put me in the same category as him.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.340
That's not my problem!

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.750
And why wouldn't I group you together?

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.500
<i>Yuki-chan's always so quick to snap back.</i>

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.630
I really stood out and was super 
popular at last year's Inter-High.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.610
You idiot, I enjoyed way 
more quiet popularity.

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.870
Your fans scream all the time.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.210
Your fans are all guys.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.390
Th-That's got nothing to do with this, moron!

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:42.590
Did you come all the way here to brag 
about yourselves to each other?

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:43.970
You seem awfully composed.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.470
<i>Is this a strategy? Or a falling out?</i>

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.400
<i>No, it doesn't matter.</i>

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.170
Road racing is a team battle!

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:53.800
Hakone Academy's making their move!

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.490
I can see that, idiot!

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:57.300
And we're on a climb.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.580
Kuroda-san may have changed roles, 
but he's a former climber.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.870
His climbing is top-class!

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:09.540
<b>Hakone Academy</b>

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.000
It's Kuroda the Climber!

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.510
He always attacks on the 
climb to finish a race!

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:09.540
He's so fast!

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.570
Come on! Come if you can, Sohoku!

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.970
I'll tear you to pieces here!

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:18.970
<i>I know about you, redheaded Naruko.</i>

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:23.430
<i>The man pulling now is a former sprinter.</i>

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.720
He's attacking on the climb!

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.060
Is Squinty for real?

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.390
Naruko's pulling for Sohoku!

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.070
<b>Spirit</b>

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:34.120
I watched him last year, but he's a sprinter!

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.410
They can't catch up!

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:36.650
They'll get left behind!

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.410
Huh?

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.240
<b>Spirit</b>

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:41.240
He's smiling?

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.450
You're attacking on the climb?

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.330
Now that's delicious.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:49.580
You know what my favorite foods are?

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:53.960
Okonomiyaki, beef tendon hotpot,
 and finally...

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:57.880
The faces of people I've amazed!

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:05.100
Naruko's Special Internally-Developed 
Armstrong Climb, Version Two!

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:09.510
He's racing up the slope so quickly, 
while swinging his handlebars side to side!

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:12.370
Sohoku's Naruko is so flashy!

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:13.980
So flashy!

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.620
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:23.740
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:49.890
<i>LINE.02 The Two Aces!!</i>

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.040
It's no use.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.810
The Armstrong Climb that 
converts my arm strength

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:55.600
into forward propulsion 
is approaching its limits.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:58.390
My time won't improve.

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:06.260
It lacks impact.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:10.840
Isn't there anything else
 I can use to power up further?

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:14.140
I'm using my arms,
and naturally, I'm using my legs.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.630
If I'm going to do something, 
I want something flashy.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:22.210
Something unthinkable that 
will really surprise people.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.170
Come to think of it,

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:35.360
my master said not to box myself in
 when trying to change something.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.380
To question common sense.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.040
<i>"Naturally, I'm using my legs."</i>

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:41.380
<i>Naturally?</i>

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:42.370
<i>Wait.</i>

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:46.420
<i>I think I'm using them, but maybe there's 
some part I'm still not utilizing.</i>

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:55.050
Oh, crap! I think I've found it!

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:56.270
I really am...

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:59.690
a genius!

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:03.900
Version Two uses the tips of my toes!

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:09.910
They may only be toes, but those 
toes will challenge common sense!

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:13.640
When turning the crank on a bike and turning 
that force into forward propulsion,

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:17.960
<b>Forward Thrust</b>

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:17.280
the effective area is 
the first quadrant only.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.920
The rest is converted 
into downward propulsion,

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:22.050
<b>Downward Thrust</b>

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.050
so it's inefficient to put 
too much strength into it.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:26.840
The first part of your body to reach that 
precious zone is the tips of your toes.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:30.430
So I strengthened my toes.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.870
That's how I amplified my power!

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.890
So I could turn my pedals even harder!

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:40.330
I raise my toes which would normally 
be pointed down and push!

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:43.820
I turn all that power into forward 
propulsion without losing any of it!

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:47.120
Thanks for challenging us on the climb.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:53.740
You wouldn't want to miss Armstrong Climb,
 Version Two: Tip-Toe Advance!

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.790
<i>This guy...</i>

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:58.410
Sohoku's Naruko caught up!

00:05:58.410 --> 00:05:59.250
On the climb!

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:01.750
Seriously? He's so fast!

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.970
That's it, Naruko!

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.470
You're so flashy!

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:07.910
What do you think?

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:10.720
I've also got something called 
the Flashy Smug Climb, too.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:11.970
Should we try it out?

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:14.940
Let's not.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.850
I get it now.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:18.570
<i>I see.</i>

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:21.050
<i>So they weren't having a falling out.</i>

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:25.780
<i>I'll have to flip my switch to finish this.</i>

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:29.280
<i>To destroy their teamwork.</i>

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.750
I have one last question.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:36.950
Sohoku, which of you two is the ace?

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.000
Yuki-chan, isn't it obvious?
 The guy behind—

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:44.450
Curious, are you?

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:45.750
Isn't it obvious?

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:50.930
I wish I could say it's our secret strategy, 
but I'll do you a favor and tell you.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:51.930
The ace is...

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:53.460
...me!

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:58.040
What? Hotshot, what are you talking about?

00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:59.690
What—Naruko! Are you serious?

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:01.250
Of course.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:05.440
I, the Red Bullet and genius 
Naruko Shoukichi, am Sohoku's ace.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.370
Calm down, Naruko. I'm the ace.

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.650
Teshima-san said the same thing.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:15.030
He was just saying that so you 
wouldn't strain yourself. Probably.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.370
No! I'm the ace!

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.730
Have you forgotten?

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:20.760
I'm the one who won the training camp!

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.760
I'm clearly better than you!

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.760
It was... close.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.170
Close, but I won!

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:27.920
<i>That's it.</i>

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:31.510
<i>These two are a hastily thrown together team.</i>

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:36.340
Wait! I thought you were pulling 
so I could save my strength!

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:38.520
Normally the man in front is the assistant!

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:39.660
You idiot!

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:41.610
I'm just doing it to stand out!

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:43.150
You'll pull for me before the finish line!

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:43.940
What?

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:45.570
What's your deal, anyway?

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:46.730
When I charged ahead...

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:50.860
That's why we've prepared our fastest man!

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.360
Isn't that what you said?

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.200
You didn't prepare me for anything!

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.890
I did!

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:59.500
I was thinking about the team's strength!

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:02.890
I did that so you could be the assistant!

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:05.420
Why do I have to assist you?

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:06.980
In any case, calm down.

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:08.280
I'm the ace.

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:09.130
No, me!

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:12.630
I'm the one who told you to
 switch from sprinter to all-rounder!

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:14.260
I made the decision!

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:22.310
<i>There are always aces and assistants 
who hastily team up during a race.</i>

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.860
<i>And they almost always break apart.</i>

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:30.150
Wait up, idiot!

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.320
Wait, Hakone Academy!

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:32.760
Don't run!

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:34.280
Where do you think you're going?

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.200
<i>They reacted. Both of them, together.</i>

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.780
Let's race, hotshot.

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:40.700
What?

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:43.270
We'll pull ahead of
Hakone Academy before the finish line.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:44.000
I see.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.170
Whoever crosses the 
finish line first is the ace!

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.420
<i>What? Are they...</i>

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.210
Bring it on!

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:53.550
Yuki-chan!

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:55.090
I know!

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.580
Let's go, Ashikiba! We're accelerating!

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:58.100
Yeah!

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:02.430
<i>They're ignoring us so 
the two of them can race?</i>

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:04.980
Don't underestimate us, Sohoku!

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.160
Teshima-san is on my side.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.000
He thinks of me as the ace.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:11.930
You idiot.

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:14.320
Every era's always looking for a new star.

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:17.530
<i>They're actually arguing with each other!</i>

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.960
Keep your voice down, Naruko.

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:22.700
Our opponents will realize we've 
never worked together before.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:23.780
What?

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:26.140
Okay, then let's pretend we're friends.

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.540
I can't do that.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.500
Hey!

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:32.060
<i>Teamwork is what's important 
before the finish line.</i>

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:35.880
<i>It's easy to break apart opponents who lack that.</i>

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:38.050
Ashikiba!

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:39.970
Yeah!

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.400
He's huge!

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:44.640
It's Hakone Academy's Ashikiba!

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:46.310
Is their ace making his move?

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:49.100
No!

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.800
It's him!

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:53.820
He distracted us with the big guy, 
disappeared to the other side,

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.860
and pulled ahead!

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.610
Crap! He's getting ahead, too!

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:01.370
They took the lead in a second!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.450
Things are back to normal now, Sohoku.

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:05.200
Seriously?

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:10.400
<i>That move is made possible by Ashikiba's 
fake-out and my explosive power.</i>

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:14.260
<i>Ashikiba's big. Everyone's 
eyes are drawn to him.</i>

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.580
<i>It's a combo only we can pull off.</i>

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.430
<i>Since this spring,
 we've been eight for eight.</i>

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.760
<i>We've achieved more!</i>

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.880
How could you let them pass you, Naruko?

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:24.840
Don't underestimate them.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:27.550
Well, you were just watching.

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:28.440
You were!

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:29.310
No, you!

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:32.730
<i>It's easy to break apart a 
hastily thrown together team.</i>

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.750
<i>Just force them into a corner.</i>

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:37.750
<i>Then they'll blame each 
other for their mistakes.</i>

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:41.290
<i>Looks like I won't have to flip my switch.</i>

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.910
You can race for third
 to decide who's the ace!

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.580
Your nonsense won't get you anywhere!

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.520
They're getting ahead again.

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:52.710
Kuroda-san's explosive power is exceptional.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:58.760
Who... will take it?

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:01.090
You mean take the lead?

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:03.530
It's either us or Hakone Academy, right?

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:06.140
I'm sure we'll do it.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:09.050
No, Naruko or Imaizumi...

00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:10.810
Which of them will take the race.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:12.060
Huh?

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:18.370
I told them to decide between 
themselves who the ace is.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:19.480
What?

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:20.850
Huh? What?

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:23.570
Do you think that was an 
irresponsible order, Onoda?

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:24.990
Huh?

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:30.960
But last year, that's how you 
dragged Sohoku into first place.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:40.920
I believe in their strength.

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:46.800
They don't get along. They're always arguing. 
They never cooperate.

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:47.640
But...

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:49.470
Yes.

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:54.900
They know better than anyone 
what they have to do.

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:56.710
Hurry up and pull, Naruko!

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:58.120
Hakone Academy's getting away!

00:11:58.120 --> 00:11:59.610
Shut up, idiot!

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.840
I'm just taking my time since 
I've got some baggage to carry.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:04.240
What? What baggage?

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:07.330
You pulled like crazy through the mountains.

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:11.250
Even for you, hotshot,
 you pushed yourself too hard.

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:12.600
Don't mention it.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:16.550
I said I'd switch with you, 
but you told me to fall back.

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:19.050
Man, I hate when people show off.

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:22.760
So now I'm pulling for you.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:27.180
And while I'm being considerate by pulling 
for you, you're reacting poorly!

00:12:27.650 --> 00:12:30.930
When I broke out my special Tip-Toe Advance,
 you just sat there and stared.

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:37.300
Don't you have anything to say?
 Like, "Wow," or, "Amazing?"

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:41.410
"This is what you've been hiding?"

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:44.040
"Seriously? This is so amazing,
 I pooped my pants!"

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:45.450
Surely you can react better than that.

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:49.200
Oh, that?

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:53.720
I thought it was only natural, 
so I wasn't surprised.

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:54.610
Huh?

00:12:55.250 --> 00:13:02.460
I knew you'd have something special 
prepared for the Inter-High.

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:08.470
You're not so dumb, hotshot!

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:12.280
Fine, let's chase them.

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:17.330
I don't like that we're doing it together, 
but there's only ever one thing to do.

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:18.230
Yeah.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:21.320
Deliver this jersey to the finish line first.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:22.480
Of course.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:25.810
We'll catch up to
 Hakone Academy and pass them!

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:27.490
You don't need to say it!

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:36.000
If we can draw out everything they have—
no, we have to to beat the champions.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.210
And this Inter-High has been 
disrupting expectations.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:43.770
There may be more than one 
opponent at the finish line.

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:47.380
<b>Feed Zone</b>

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:49.690
What is that?

00:13:49.690 --> 00:13:51.220
They're carrying water bottles!

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:52.450
Excuse us!

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:53.580
Coming through!

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:54.550
Hurry, Sugimoto!

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:55.810
They're almost here!

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.480
Yes, sir!

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:01.350
We made it.

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:03.440
Imaizumi!

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:04.110
Naruko!

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:05.780
We'll just take the water!

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:12.120
Imaizumi, Naruko!

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:13.790
Go, Sohoku!

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:13.810
You can do it!

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:16.040
Imaizumi!

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:19.040
You don't need to shout so loud, Sugimoto.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.460
I can hear you. Don't worry.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:25.530
The finish line...

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:26.210
...will be...

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:28.710
...mine!

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:33.850
Imaizumi...

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:37.400
<i>The finish line is less 
than ten kilometers away.</i>

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:38.490
<i>It's right there.</i>

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:44.110
<i>If my feelings can help you in any way,
 then I'll pray as hard as I can.</i>

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:47.990
<i>Take it. I'm counting on you, Imaizumi.</i>

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:50.370
Let's head back to the tent, Sugimoto.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:52.610
Yes, Koga-san.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:55.460
The rest should be coming soon.

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:59.080
Kaburagi and the others will have met up 
with Onoda and Teshima by now.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.630
It'll be hard for the two of us to 
hand out supplies for four riders.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:05.480
I see. You're right.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:08.550
But I'm glad we made it 
to the feed zone in time.

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:10.380
Yeah.

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:14.890
We carried everyone's supplies 
here on the spare bikes.

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:18.110
It was hard, but...

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:23.770
I know it wasn't the official course,
but I'm glad to have ridden at the Inter-High.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:25.940
I rode as hard as I could.

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:30.900
All I could think about was getting 
here in time, but now I'm numb.

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:33.350
It's exciting, isn't it?

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:36.530
Next year, I'll work harder 
so I can be in the Inter-High—

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:40.630
<i>Koga-san is a third-year.</i>

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:43.750
<i>This is his last Inter-High.</i>

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:45.620
I'm sorry.

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:47.560
Don't worry about it, Sugimoto.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:50.260
Will you be in next year's Inter-High?

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:53.770
Then you'll have to practice hard.

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:57.380
Remember how the Inter-High feels.

00:15:57.970 --> 00:15:59.770
But we have work to do first.

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:01.520
Let's hand out supplies to—

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:06.470
What? Support staff are on the course?

00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:07.850
Huh? Kyoto?

00:16:07.850 --> 00:16:08.780
But why?

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:11.610
Did they get them mixed up
 with Hakone Academy?

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:15.450
You were in the same position as Sohoku.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:18.370
You didn't hear the correction on the radio?

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:22.410
They shook off the others.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:25.680
I hate to think we were outmatched.

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:28.460
And even if they've gone, there's no 
guarantee they'll make it to the front.

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:31.040
But it's true that they're pursuing them.

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:32.720
I trust our riders...

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:38.220
But they say Kyoto's Midousuji 
was tricky last year, too.

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:40.900
B-By himself?

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:45.850
This year there's two of 
them chasing the leaders!

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:49.820
Kyoto Fushimi #111, the ace, Midousuji Akira!

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:53.820
And #116, first-year Kishigami Komari!

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:55.320
<i>Him!</i>

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:01.930
Their roster said he was a sub.

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.160
Rumor was he was a masseuse.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:06.170
<i>He races?</i>

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:12.640
You're really not riding in the Inter-High.

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:16.010
But you had such fine muscles!

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:19.420
Go, Fushimi!

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:21.390
Pedal, Kishigami!

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:23.900
<i>What was that?</i>

00:17:23.900 --> 00:17:26.070
<i>Those weren't the eyes of 
a man aiming for victory.</i>

00:17:26.070 --> 00:17:29.400
<i>No, they didn't go for the 
sprint or mountains, either.</i>

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:33.670
<i>Has Kyoto Fushimi set their sights 
on only the finish line again?</i>

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:36.360
<i>Be careful, Imaizumi and Naruko.</i>

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.320
<i>They intend to catch up.</i>

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:41.970
Would you like to move up, Komari-kun?

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:43.730
Yes, of course.

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:46.710
I'll pull. I want to reach the 
front as soon as possible.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:51.200
There are so many fine muscles 
at the front, right?

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:54.710
Oh, the muscles. The muscles...

00:17:56.050 --> 00:18:01.640
<i>Komari-kun, you really 
are a man of no patience.</i>

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:09.240
<i>It took only a moment.</i>

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:15.440
<i>They were waiting for the momentary loss 
of focus when we prepared to resupply.</i>

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:19.200
<i>I was cautious.</i>

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:23.030
<i>I knew Kyoto would go for the 
finish line again this year.</i>

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:26.900
<i>I knew they'd make their 
move before the feed zone.</i>

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:27.890
<i>But...</i>

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:30.840
They passed us! Doubashi!

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.130
Kaburagi, go!

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:33.590
They passed right between us!

00:18:35.140 --> 00:18:36.460
Stop Kyoto!

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:45.520
See?

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:50.920
Because you wasted all your 
energy on a stupid sprint,

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:55.160
you got caught during a crucial moment!

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:56.570
Damn!

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:58.990
Damn!

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:05.290
They're going for the finish line.

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:09.700
<i>Be careful, Imaizumi-kun and Naruko-kun.</i>

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:14.670
We're starting to catch up to Hakone Academy!

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:17.170
It's only 4,500 meters to the finish line!

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:22.010
Final stop coming up.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:25.600
The Naruko Super Express is heading 
straight to the finish line.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:27.890
Good. I'm taking this train.

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:29.570
You can't ride for free, idiot.

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:31.090
It'll cost you ten billion yen.

00:19:31.090 --> 00:19:33.480
That's cheap. Do you accept cash?

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:36.500
Ugh, gross. That's what rich people say.

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:37.650
I was joking.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:40.340
You're such a hotshot,
 I didn't think you were joking!

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:41.650
I bet you don't have any friends!

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:43.240
There's Onoda, and...

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:46.410
You really don't have any friends!

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:48.490
Want me to be your friend?

00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:49.720
A special, just for you.

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:50.690
No, I'm good.

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:53.750
I call anyone whose house 
I've been to a friend.

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:56.040
Seriously? Those are kid rules!

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:57.890
Call it whatever you want.

00:19:57.890 --> 00:20:02.380
Down to the smallest things, 
I determine my own standards!

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:05.970
<i>Hotshot.</i>

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:10.890
The ace Imaizumi moved ahead 
with 4000 meters remaining!

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:12.180
We're accelerating!

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:14.560
Try not to fall behind, Naruko!

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:16.230
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:20:17.140 --> 00:20:20.490
I'm the genius all-rounder, Naruko Shoukichi!

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:23.370
These guys...

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:26.110
<i>Imaizumi moved ahead and is accelerating?</i>

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:28.570
<i>Don't they know about 
saving the ace's strength?</i>

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:29.740
<i>They're total amateurs!</i>

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:32.000
I'm the ace!

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:35.460
<i>Do they not care who wins since 
they haven't chosen an ace?</i>

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:39.880
Fools. You're complete fools.

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:41.260
Yuki-chan.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:45.600
<i>You have no idea what position you're in.</i>

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:47.110
<i>I'll show you.</i>

00:20:47.110 --> 00:20:49.470
<i>I'll make you understand.</i>

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.160
<i>How dare they underestimate us.</i>

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:53.350
<i>I'll flip my switch.</i>

00:20:54.770 --> 00:21:00.650
You think you can beat us 
with your desperate strategy?

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:02.700
Two times one is two.

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:04.400
Two times two is four.

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:06.320
Two times three is six.

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:07.820
Two times four is eight.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.510
Two times five is ten.

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:11.290
Two times six is 12.

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.120
Two times seven is 14.

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:15.140
Two times eight is 16.

00:21:15.140 --> 00:21:17.170
Two times nine is 18.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:18.980
They're teeming with muscles!

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:23.590
Mi...

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:25.170
<i>Midousuji...</i>

00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:26.800
<i>Kyoto Fushimi...</i>

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:29.190
<i>Such incredible pressure!</i>

00:21:29.190 --> 00:21:33.270
<i>He looks unbelievably huge!</i>

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:36.760
We caught up!

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:09.990
Sendoff Race Strategy Meeting

00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:12.120
Arakita-san should make his move right away.

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:14.490
Then Ashikiba and I can...

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:18.610
I see. You'll take the lead 
before the finish line, and—

00:23:19.880 --> 00:23:21.220
Oh, sorry.

00:23:25.770 --> 00:23:27.260
C-Continue.

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:30.800
Touichirou, if you've got 
something to say, spit it out.

00:23:31.320 --> 00:23:33.970
Yuki-chan, what's this in front of me?

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:34.760
A mushroom?

00:23:34.760 --> 00:23:36.130
It's me!

00:23:36.490 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>NEXT LINE The Appointed Time</i>

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:51.250
<b>Mura</b>
